{% doc %}
  The pixel size of an icon, resolved from a keyword.

  ## One vocabulary, one place that decides what it means

  Every icon control in the theme used to be a slider with a range of its own —
  16–96 on a badge, 10–32 on a button, 12–48 on a subheading — so **Icon size**
  meant something different in each panel, the same number looked different in
  two of them, and nothing lined up across a page. The control is now the same
  five steps plus **Custom** everywhere, the way **Button size** already works,
  and the steps are resolved here rather than in nine blocks.

  ## The steps are the theme's own numbers

      extra_small  12px
      small        Theme settings › Colors › Icon sizes › Small   (14px)
      medium       …› Medium                                      (20px), the default
      large        …› Large                                       (28px)
      extra_large  40px

  Small, Medium and Large read theme settings rather than hard-coding a ladder
  here, so a store that resizes its icons moves every block with them. Extra
  small and Extra large are the ends of those same option lists — 12 is the
  smallest Small offers, 40 the largest Large does — so the ladder never leaves
  the range the theme already sanctions, and there is no fourth and fifth
  setting to keep in order with the other three.

  ## A stored number still works

  Blocks kept a px number in `icon_size` before the keywords existed. Such a
  value is passed through rather than snapped to the nearest step, so updating
  the theme never resizes an icon a merchant had already set by hand.

  @param {string} [size] - extra_small | small | medium | large | extra_large | custom. A bare px number is passed through.
  @param {number} [custom] - The block's own **Custom size**, used when `size` is `custom`.

  @example
    {%- liquid
      capture icon_px
        render 'icon-size', size: s.icon_size, custom: s.icon_size_custom
      endcapture
      assign icon_size = icon_px | plus: 0
    -%}
{% enddoc %}

{%- liquid
  assign px_sm = settings.icon_size_sm | default: 14 | plus: 0
  assign px_md = settings.icon_size_md | default: 20 | plus: 0
  assign px_lg = settings.icon_size_lg | default: 28 | plus: 0

  assign resolved = px_md
  assign key = size | default: 'medium'

  case key
    when 'extra_small'
      assign resolved = 12
    when 'small'
      assign resolved = px_sm
    when 'medium'
      assign resolved = px_md
    when 'large'
      assign resolved = px_lg
    when 'extra_large'
      assign resolved = 40
    when 'custom'
      assign resolved = custom | default: px_md | plus: 0
    else
      comment
        A px number from a template written before the keywords, or a keyword a
        schema no longer offers. Only the first survives `plus: 0` as anything
        other than zero, so only the first is honoured.
      endcomment
      assign stored = key | plus: 0
      if stored > 0
        assign resolved = stored
      endif
  endcase
-%}
{{- resolved -}}
